<span class="status">Research framework · Python · Demonstration</span>
<h3>AI Search Visibility Lab</h3>
<p>A reproducible framework for controlled query sets, brand visibility measurement, citation and retrieval analysis, automated reporting and testing.</p>
<ul><li>Structured prompt/query datasets</li><li>Visibility and citation metrics</li><li>Evidence provenance</li><li>Python reporting and tests</li></ul><a class="repo-link" href="https://github.com/federicaiengo/data-analytics-portfolio/tree/main/projects/ai-search-visibility-lab" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect source code ↗</a>
</article>
<a class="card project-card" href="/projects/seo-aeo-geo-optimization/">
<span class="status">Independent case study · Proposed interventions</span>
<h3>SEO/AEO/GEO Optimization</h3>
<p>A real public-site research subject taken from baseline through diagnosis, query fan-out, entity analysis and proposed optimization.</p>
<ul><li>12 frozen baseline prompts</li><li>Answerability and citability audit</li><li>Six intervention candidates</li><li>Before → proposed redesign examples</li></ul>
<span class="open">Read case study →</span>
</a>
<a class="card project-card" href="/projects/ai-search-competitive-intelligence/">
<span class="status">Benchmark protocol · Observations pending</span>
<h3>AI Search Competitive Intelligence</h3>
<p>A controlled comparison of Notion, Asana, ClickUp and monday.com designed to keep first-party evidence separate from AI observations.</p>
<ul><li>35 frozen prompts</li><li>Seven intent families</li><li>Capability and pricing baselines</li><li>Auditable scoring rules</li></ul>
