<section class="project-group">
<div class="group-heading"><p class="eyebrow">Data Engineering · Analytics</p><h2>Reliable pipelines, clear results</h2></div>
<div class="grid data-grid">
<article class="card project-card"><span class="status">Data Engineering · Python · Snowflake · dbt · Power BI</span><h3>E-Commerce Revenue & Operations Analytics</h3><p>End-to-end pipeline from Python/pandas and Snowflake ingestion through 28 dbt models to a four-page Power BI report.</p><ul><li>249/249 passing dbt regression tests</li><li>99,441 modeled orders</li><li>303 payment-value mismatches investigated</li><li>Incremental MERGE and idempotent reruns</li></ul><a class="repo-link" href="/projects/ecommerce-technical-evidence/">Read the evidence-led case study →</a><br><a class="repo-link" href="https://github.com/federicaiengo/data-analytics-portfolio/tree/main/projects/ecommerce-revenue-operations-analytics" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect project, code & report ↗</a></article>
<article class="card project-card"><span class="status">PostgreSQL · SQL · Tableau</span><h3>Insurance Claims Analytics</h3><p>PostgreSQL and SQL audit of 10,000 insurance claims, covering financial exposure, severity, concentration and referential integrity. Includes an executive Tableau dashboard.</p><ul><li>10,000 claims across related datasets</li><li>Data quality and referential integrity</li><li>Agent and vendor exposure</li><li>Executive Tableau dashboard</li></ul><a class="repo-link" href="/projects/insurance-claims-evidence/">Read the evidence-led case study →</a><br><a class="repo-link" href="https://github.com/federicaiengo/data-analytics-portfolio/tree/main/projects/insurance-claims-analytics" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect project & dashboard ↗</a></article>
<article class="card project-card"><span class="status">SQL · HR analytics · In progress</span><h3>HR Analytics: Employee Attrition</h3><p>What can employee data tell us about turnover? An analysis of 1,470 records explores overtime, job roles and job satisfaction, while distinguishing patterns in a sample dataset from proven causes.</p><ul><li>30.53% attrition among overtime employees versus 10.44% without overtime</li><li>Role and department comparisons</li><li>Documented limitations and next investigations</li><li>Source-audited 1,470-row cleaned dataset (32 columns)</li><li>Static Excel dashboard; desktop compatibility QA pending</li></ul><a class="repo-link" href="/projects/hr-attrition-evidence/">Read the work-in-progress findings →</a><br><a class="repo-link" href="https://github.com/federicaiengo/data-analytics-portfolio/tree/main/projects/hr-analytics-employee-attrition" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect project evidence ↗</a></article>
</div>
</section>

<section class="method">
<p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
<h2>Reproducibility is part of the deliverable.</h2>
<p>Where a project uses a benchmark, the prompts and scoring rules are fixed before results are interpreted. Where it uses public evidence, observations and inference stay separate. Where it uses data, transformations and quality checks are documented rather than hidden behind a final chart.</p>
</section>
